    "lastText": "I built `ledger` as TASK.md describes. All 13 acceptance criteria in `.goal/SPEC.md` pass, including `npm test` (36 tests, none skipped). The auditor re-ran the checks, tried the CLI by hand against TASK.md, found no gaps and no gamed tests, and returned VERDICT: PASS.\n\nEverything is in `bin/ledger.js`, `src/`, `test/` and `README.md`, with no npm dependencies.\n\nTwo behaviours TASK.md doesn't settle, and what I chose:\n- **`--times 1`:** `add --repeat monthly --times 1` prints `added #<id>` rather than `added #1..#1`.\n- **`undo` after `add`:** undoing an `add` also rolls back the id counter, so that id can be handed out again. Ids are still never reused after `delete`.\n\nTwo of my own tests had bugs on the first run: a wrong expected order in `test/io.test.js` and a typo in `test/errors.test.js`. I fixed the tests, not the code.\n\nSTATUS 13/13 verified",
